+of the GNU General Public License.
+
+## Why GPL-3.0?
+
+The dependency chain is:
+
+```
+Foundation-Devices/iso14443-rs    GPL-3.0-or-later
+  └─ Amperstrand/iso14443-rs      GPL-3.0-or-later (forced — derivative work)
+      ├─ bolty-rs                 GPL-3.0-or-later (forced — static linking)
+      └─ ccid-firmware-rs         GPL-2.0-or-later → effectively GPL-3.0-or-later
+```
+
+Rust crates are statically compiled into the final binary. Static linking with
+GPL-3.0 code requires the combined work to also be GPL-3.0-or-later. There is
+no LGPL or dynamic-link exception in the upstream license.
+
+## What this means for downstream projects
+
+Any project that depends on this crate (directly or transitively) must be
+distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later or a compatible license (e.g., GPL-3.0-only,
+AGPL-3.0). Permissive licenses like MIT or Apache-2.0 are NOT sufficient when
+statically linking GPL-3.0 code.
+
+Commercial use, modification, and redistribution are all permitted under
+GPL-3.0, provided that the complete corresponding source code is made
+available to recipients.
